        "text": "The fix is straightforward. The old code used:\n\n```python\nend = start + per_page - 1\n```\n\nThis made the slice non-inclusive of the last item that should be on the page, because Python slice `items[start:end]` already excludes `end`. Removing the `- 1` so that `end = start + per_page` gives the correct half-open interval.\n\n**Fix:** Changed `end = start + per_page - 1` \u2192 `end = start + per_page`.\n\nAll four test cases now pass:\n\n| Page | Before (dropped last) | After (correct) |\n|------|----------------------|-----------------|\n| 1, 3 | `[0, 1]` | `[0, 1, 2]` |\n| 2, 3 | `[3, 4]` | `[3, 4, 5]` |\n| 4, 3 | `[]` | `[9]` |\n| 9, 3 | `[]` | `[]` |",
